# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Contentful photo sync — secrets, cache, and generated images
# .env.* too: backups (.env.bak) and per-environment files (.env.local,
# .env.production) all hold the same secrets and were previously tracked.
# .env.example is the committed template and must stay visible.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Google service-account keys. The downloaded file is a long-lived
# credential with no expiry — it belongs outside the repo entirely, and
# in .env as base64 (npm run key). These patterns are a backstop for the
# names Google hands out, in case one gets dropped in here by accident.
project-*.json
*service-account*.json
*-key.json
.drive-cache.json
public/photos/*
# ...but keep the design-project cover screenshots (npm run shoot): they're
# stable, hand-generated assets that must ship with the repo, not build-time
# Contentful output.
!public/photos/web/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
